            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Samuel J. Buffone, Esq., on behalf of the Petitioner, petitioner F. Scott Yeager argues that a jury\u2019s acquittal on any issue is final and bars the government from seeking a contrary determination on that issue."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a424ed6dde87ec6cf4694435c79bcb30eaaa00c1ed9d93ee1d592790c647b1b5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a424ed6dde87-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent, the United States contends that the government may retry hung counts that occur alongside acquittals, invoking the doctrine of continuing jeopardy."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Samuel J. Buffone, Esq., on behalf of the Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a424ed6dde87ec6cf4694435c79bcb30eaaa00c1ed9d93ee1d592790c647b1b5",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a424ed6dde87-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Samuel J. Buffone, Esq., on behalf of the Petitioner, petitioner asserts that an acquittal resolves the issue in the defendant\u2019s favor and is final, preventing the government from obtaining an inconsistent determination."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a424ed6dde87ec6cf4694435c79bcb30eaaa00c1ed9d93ee1d592790c647b1b5",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a424ed6dde87-0002-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 49,
                "start": 49
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioner further argues that the Double Jeopardy Clause should be applied with reason and a non\u2011hypertechnical view to protect the public policies underlying the Clause."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a424ed6dde87ec6cf4694435c79bcb30eaaa00c1ed9d93ee1d592790c647b1b5",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a424ed6dde87-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 21,
                "start": 21
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, the United States argues that the government may retry hung counts that occur with acquittals, based on the doctrine of continuing jeopardy which allows the government one full and fair opportunity to convict."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a424ed6dde87ec6cf4694435c79bcb30eaaa00c1ed9d93ee1d592790c647b1b5",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a424ed6dde87-0002-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 48,
                "start": 48
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The Government also maintains that collateral estoppel requires a rational jury verdict, referencing Ashe v. Swenson."
        }
      ],
